<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="safemode_help.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <!-- safe mode wildcard help, sounds (SOUND category). A passive backdrop stacked
         UNDER the string_input "Safe Mode Rule:" popup, replacing the curses help
         window. Static: no data model. Literal English with column alignment preserved
         (white-space: pre), matching the curses readout and the same i18n gap noted
         for the column heads. -->
    <div class="panel smh-panel">
        <div class="smh-text">* is used as a Wildcard.  A few Examples:

footsteps      matches the sound name exactly
a loud ba*     matches sounds beginning with 'a loud ba'
*losion!       matches sounds ending with 'losion!'
a *oud*ba*     multiple * are allowed
*LoU*bA*       case insensitive search</div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
